sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as User
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant BE as Backend API
    participant Trigger as Trigger Layer
    participant StatusDB as Status Database
    participant Compute as Compute Layer

    User->>FE: Click Run on the job configuration page
    FE->>BE: Send run request with job id, inputs, and current user context
    BE->>StatusDB: Create run record with status queued and request metadata
    StatusDB-->>BE: Return persisted run id and initial status snapshot
    BE->>Trigger: Publish run event with run id and execution payload
    Trigger-->>BE: Acknowledge trigger accepted for asynchronous execution
    BE-->>FE: Return run id and queued status for immediate UI update
    FE-->>User: Show run started state with queued status and run identifier
    Trigger->>Compute: Start compute job with normalized payload and runtime config
    Compute->>StatusDB: Update run status to running with worker metadata and start time
    StatusDB-->>Compute: Confirm running status persisted
    Compute->>Compute: Execute workload and stream intermediate progress internally
    Compute->>StatusDB: Persist final outputs, completion time, and succeeded status
    StatusDB-->>Compute: Confirm final state persisted
    FE->>BE: Poll latest run status using run id
    BE->>StatusDB: Read latest status and result summary for run id
    StatusDB-->>BE: Return succeeded status, timestamps, and output summary
    BE-->>FE: Return completed status payload for UI refresh
    FE-->>User: Show run completed state with latest output summary
